        FIXBIN.EXE filename.ext loadaddress data

        Fixbin allows you to replace data at "loadaddress" with the data
        specified in "data". The file can be any file, including ascii,
        but you have to know the load address for your data.
        eg. fixbin test.bin 12ac 01ff02fe03fd04fc05fb06fa07ee08
        Opens file test.bin if it exists and seeks byte number 12ac(hex).
        Replaces what is there with the binary data, 
        "01ff02fe03fd04fc05fb06fa07ee08". It displays the replaced data
        as well as the replacing data.
        The syntax must be specified exactly as above, where the load-
        address is in ascii-hex and separates the filename and the data
        with a single space between each. The data is also ascii-hex and
        may not have a space separating bytes.
